\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus shall reign where'er the sun
\par Doth his successive journeys run ;
\par His kingdom stretch from shore to shore,
\par Till suns shall rise and set no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Him shall endless prayer be made,
\par And praises throng to crown His head ; 
\par His name like sweet perfume shall rise
\par With every morning sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. People and realms prayer be made,
\par Dwell on His love with sweetest song ;
\par And infant voices shall proclaim
\par Their young hosannas to His name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Blessings abound wher'er He reigns ;
\par The prisoner leaps to lose his chains ;
\par The weary find eternal rest ;
\par And all the sons of want are blest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Where He displays His healing power,
\par Death and the curse are known no more ;
\par In Him the tribes of Adam boast
\par More blessings than their father lost.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Let every creature rise, and bring
\par Its grateful honours to our King ;
\par Angels descend with songs again,
\par And earth prolong the joyful strain.\tab 
\par                                             Amen.
\par \i 
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

